+    "hardness_basis": (
+        "Track B: Remark 11.1(ii) names the polynomial Euclidean algorithm; "
+        "the implemented reference route uses generic binary modular powers, "
+        "a geometric sum, and extended Euclid in O(E^2(log n+log N)+E^3) "
+        "exact rational operations, measured at the shipping preset at 16,288 "
+        "operations and 0.109 seconds on average over eight seeds, while the "
+        "roots-of-unity coefficient permutation takes 228 operations and must "
