There is a substantial pre-existing draft in the workspace, so I’m treating it as untrusted and auditing it rather than starting over. Its core construction is legitimate: it carries a closed Bézout witness through quotient-ring automorphisms and affine variable changes, while verification recomputes the polynomial congruence exactly. I’ve already found metadata and measurement details that need correction, and the mandatory oracle files currently contain only OpenRouter 403 errors—those do not establish hardness.
