One audit correction matters for G4: because the displayed scale \(g\) makes “coefficients are multiples of \(g\)” a natural solver prior, the random-guess experiment should sample that smaller lattice, not the much looser full integer box. I’m tightening the declared certificate language and rerunning density against this stronger prior. I’m also fixing the canonical key to include the target and language bound, so instances with the same quotient residue but different right-hand sides are not over-collapsed.
