 ## Caveats
 
-This family is easy with a CAS or any polynomial extended-GCD implementation;
-that is the declared Track B reference algorithm.  It also becomes short by
-hand as soon as the solver recognizes the quotient invariant—the intended
-thing being tested.  The G4 probability is uniform over every bounded integer
-coefficient polynomial and is not a posterior over solver strategies.  To
-probe the construction prior, the G6 random restart samples coefficients as
-multiples of the displayed scale `g`; its smaller effective space is still
-(44^{22}\approx1.43\times10^{36}), but only 256 restarts per seed were run.
-The panel did not run a separate Gröbner-basis package because univariate
-extended Euclid is the stronger natural algorithm here.  Most importantly,
-the mandatory four-vendor model evidence is absent due to the external key
-limit; local gates alone do not establish the requested model hardness.
+This family is easy for a CAS or any implementation of extended Euclid; that is the declared Track B reference route. It may also be easy for a no-tool solver that immediately recognizes and accurately executes the roots-of-unity coefficient permutation. The guess probability measures only the explicitly bounded, scale-aware prior `w_j=g*z_j` with nonzero `|z_j|<=E-1`; it does not imply computational or model hardness. Wall time is machine-dependent, and the operation count treats an exact rational coefficient operation as one operation even when operands contain thousands of bits.
+
+The attack panel covers magnitude/sign outliers, a left-to-right greedy rule, flat and untransformed ansätze, and 256 scale-aware random restarts. It does not test every symbolic simplifier, Gröbner-basis implementation, or language model. The canonical key normalizes the declared affine-coordinate and `A`-multiple symmetries, not every possible automorphism of a rational polynomial quotient. Most importantly, the four-vendor hardening and the G9 comparison remain unmeasured because of the external 403 quota failure; this directory is ready for a rerun but is not yet valid evidence for a shipped hard instance.
