(m,n):=(Y,1), \ \ q:=c, \ \ X:=b, \ \ (y_1,y_2):=(Z,z), \\ 
E:=3, \ \ N:=\frac{Y-1}{3}, \ \ e:=\nu_{c}\bigg(\frac{Y-1}{3}\bigg), \ \ \delta:=0.
\end{gather*}
Note that $z>e$ by Lemma \ref{lem-EucAlg-Krelations}.

First, we shall check condition (II) in Proposition $\ref{prop-EuAl}$:% 
\[
\frac{(z-e)(Y-4)+2}{Y} \ge \frac{\log 2}{\log c}.

