I’m also strengthening G8 before finalizing. The solver-facing condition depends only on \(F \bmod A\), so multiplying both sides by a common nonzero scalar, adding whole \(E\)-periods to the huge exponent, or changing \(N\) by an odd common factor can leave the witness problem unchanged. The canonical key should collapse those representations; retaining their raw magnitudes would overstate diversity.
