codex
Implemented a self-contained Track‑B polynomial Bézout witness generator based on [Section 11 of the paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2604.18991v2#S11).

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2604.18991/gen_2604_18991.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2604.18991/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2604.18991/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2604.18991/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2604.18991/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2604.18991/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Results:

- All nine local gates pass.
- 744 additional instances matched independent polynomial extended Euclid.
- Reference route: 2,029,486 mean exact operations.
- Compact route: 288 operations.
- G4: 0/200,000 guesses; exact density \(1.12\times10^{-49}\).
- G8: 160/160 transformations verified and canonicalized.
- G9: 666 worst-case characters, 309 measured tokens, 84 atoms.

The required oracle hardening remains externally blocked: the configured OpenRouter key has zero remaining quota, so all 12 calls returned HTTP 403. These are correctly recorded as errors—not model failures—and establish no hardness verdict. Replenishing the key and rerunning `harden.py` is the only remaining step.
